    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Greeting one person or many",
     "texto": [
      "In English, «good morning» stays the same whether you greet one person or a group, and Chinese greetings have no plural either. **大家好** means «hello, everyone»: 大家 («everyone») goes before 好 («well; hello»)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
